WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.940
- Taylor, you're from Pennsylvania,

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.780
but after 10 years being
in Chicago regularly,

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.317
do you feel like a Chicagoan now?

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:08.330
- Yeah, I mean, like you said,

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.410
it's been almost a decade.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.150
We're in season nine.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.090
I do get a lot of,

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.960
if I get recognized, it's
mostly from my character.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.060
- Well, has just being on "Chicago Fire"

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.470
helped you get out of any jams
with Chicago law enforcement?

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.720
Have you pulled the card?

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.490
- I haven't like, I haven't
really pulled the card.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.980
Like I have met and know a
lot of first responders now,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.010
just because of, you know, proximity.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.360
But I do have a story.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.530
I was on my motorcycle, it
was raining, it was cold.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.270
The traffic was really, really bad.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.400
This was maybe two years ago.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.280
And so I hopped off onto the median

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.370
to the right side and just
started passing all the traffic,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.400
all the cars

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.900
in what would be either
a bus or service lane.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.190
A cop car gets behind me, sees me,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.090
puts the lights on, pulls me over.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.610
I think I'm, you know, gonna
get ticketed and trouble.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.800
Police officer walks up,
I take off my helmet,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.570
and he's like, "Oh, it's you,

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.170
the fake firefighter."

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.440
And we kinda laughed and had a chuckle.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.020
I think he made fun of
me for a little bit,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.430
which is fine 'cause then he let me go.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.180
He just said, "Get home safe,

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.500
don't do that again,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.310
and I like the show."

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.296
So that, you know, that's my
get out of jail free card.

00:01:25.296 --> 00:01:26.440
- That's awesome.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.323
That's amazing.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.160
You just take your helmet
off, and it's handled.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.513
That's amazing. (laughs)

